/-!
# Algebra maps over a directed colimit of rings come from a finite level

Proof of Stacks 05N8. Let `A` be a ring, `B`, `C` two `A`-algebras and `R = colim_i R_i` a
directed colimit of `A`-algebras. The mechanism behind all four items is that
`B ⊗_A R = colim_i B ⊗_A R_i`, which here takes the shape of two statements about the
comparison maps `rTensor M (g i) : R_i ⊗_A M → R ⊗_A M`: every element of `R ⊗_A M` comes from
some `R_i ⊗_A M`, and two elements of `R_i ⊗_A M` with the same image in `R ⊗_A M` already agree
in `R_j ⊗_A M` for some `j ≥ i`. Both are deduced from the corresponding statements for
`R = colim_i R_i` itself by `TensorProduct.directLimitLeft`, that tensor product commutes with
direct limits of modules.

Items (1) and (2) are then the finitely many generators of `B`, resp. `C`, caught at a finite
level. Item (3) is the source's argument: a presentation `A[x_1, …, x_m] → C` with kernel
generated by `f_1, …, f_t` turns an `A`-algebra map `C → B ⊗_A R` into finitely many elements of
`B ⊗_A R`, lifted to some `B ⊗_A R_i`, and the finitely many relations `f_s` are then satisfied
after increasing `i`. Item (4) is item (3) applied to the inverse of `u ⊗ 1`, together with the
generator computation of item (1) on both sides.

## Main results

* `Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraMapDescent.solution`: the statement of Stacks Tag 05N8.

## Implementation notes

Item (3) is proved through
`Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraMapDescent.exists_lift_of_finitePresentation`, which produces the
`A`-algebra map `C → R_i ⊗_A B` rather than the `R_i`-algebra map `R_i ⊗_A C → R_i ⊗_A B`; the
latter is recovered by `Algebra.TensorProduct.lift`, and the commuting square asked for in the statement
is exactly the statement that the two maps agree on the elements `1 ⊗ c`. Item (4) uses the same
`A`-algebra map, so it does not go through item (3)'s conclusion.

## References

* [StacksProject 05N8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05N8)
-/



open scoped TensorProduct

namespace Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraMapDescent

/-- In a directed preorder, finitely many monotone eventually-true predicates are simultaneously
true at a single index above any prescribed one. -/
private theorem exists_forall_of_forall_exists {ι : Type*} [Preorder ι] [IsDirectedOrder ι]
    {β : Type*} (i₀ : ι) (u : Finset β) (P : ι → β → Prop)
    (hmono : ∀ ⦃j k : ι⦄, j ≤ k → ∀ b, P j b → P k b) (h : ∀ b ∈ u, ∃ j, P j b) :
    ∃ j, i₀ ≤ j ∧ ∀ b ∈ u, P j b := by
  classical
  have : Nonempty ι := ⟨i₀⟩
  choose j hj using fun b : {x // x ∈ u} ↦ h b.1 b.2
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := (insert i₀ (Finset.image j Finset.univ)).exists_le
  refine ⟨M, hM i₀ (Finset.mem_insert_self _ _), fun b hb ↦ hmono ?_ b (hj ⟨b, hb⟩)⟩
  exact hM _ (Finset.mem_insert_of_mem (Finset.mem_image_of_mem j (Finset.mem_univ _)))

/-- Like `exists_forall_of_forall_exists`, for predicates that depend on a proof of `i₀ ≤ j`. -/
private theorem exists_forall_le_of_forall_exists {ι : Type*} [Preorder ι] [IsDirectedOrder ι]
    {β : Type*} (i₀ : ι) (u : Finset β) (Q : ∀ j, i₀ ≤ j → β → Prop)
    (hmono : ∀ j k (h : i₀ ≤ j) (hjk : j ≤ k) b, Q j h b → Q k (h.trans hjk) b)
    (h : ∀ b ∈ u, ∃ j h, Q j h b) : ∃ j, ∃ h : i₀ ≤ j, ∀ b ∈ u, Q j h b := by
  obtain ⟨j, hj, hall⟩ := exists_forall_of_forall_exists i₀ u (fun j b ↦ ∃ h : i₀ ≤ j, Q j h b)
    (fun j k hjk b ⟨h, hb⟩ ↦ ⟨h.trans hjk, hmono j k h hjk b hb⟩) h
  exact ⟨j, hj, fun b hb ↦ (hall b hb).choose_spec⟩

section Ext

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {S : Type*} [CommRing S] [Algebra A S]
  {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] {X : Type*} [CommRing X] [Algebra A X] [Algebra S X]
  [IsScalarTower A S X]

/-- Two `S`-algebra maps out of `S ⊗[A] B` agree as soon as they agree on the elements `1 ⊗ b`
for `b` in a set generating `B` as an `A`-algebra. -/
private theorem algHom_ext_of_adjoin_eq_top {b : Set B} (hb : Algebra.adjoin A b = ⊤)
    {φ ψ : S ⊗[A] B →ₐ[S] X} (h : ∀ x ∈ b, φ (1 ⊗ₜ x) = ψ (1 ⊗ₜ x)) : φ = ψ := by
  exact Algebra.TensorProduct.ext (Subsingleton.elim _ _)
    (AlgHom.ext_of_adjoin_eq_top hb fun x hx ↦ by simpa using h x hx)

/-- An `S`-subalgebra of `S ⊗[A] C` containing every `1 ⊗ c` with `c` in a set generating `C` as
an `A`-algebra is everything. -/
private theorem subalgebra_eq_top_of_one_tmul_mem {C : Type*} [CommRing C] [Algebra A C]
    {c : Set C} (hc : Algebra.adjoin A c = ⊤) (T : Subalgebra S (S ⊗[A] C))
    (h : ∀ x ∈ c, (1 : S) ⊗ₜ[A] x ∈ T) : T = ⊤ := by
  have h1 : ∀ x : C, (1 : S) ⊗ₜ[A] x ∈ T := fun x ↦ by
    have hx := Algebra.adjoin_le (S := (T.restrictScalars A).comap
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight (R := A) (A := S) (B := C))) (s := c)
      (fun x hx ↦ by simpa using h x hx) (hc ▸ Algebra.mem_top : x ∈ Algebra.adjoin A c)
    simpa using hx
  refine eq_top_iff.2 fun z _ ↦ ?_
  induction z with
  | tmul x y => simpa [TensorProduct.smul_tmul'] using T.smul_mem (h1 y) x
  | add z₁ z₂ hz₁ hz₂ => exact add_mem (hz₁ Algebra.mem_top) (hz₂ Algebra.mem_top)

/-- If `Ψ : C → S ⊗[A] B` inverts `u : B → C` on generators of `B` and of `C` after base change to
`S`, then `u` becomes bijective after base change to `S`. -/
private theorem lTensor_bijective_of_generators {C : Type*} [CommRing C] [Algebra A C]
    {b : Set B} (hb : Algebra.adjoin A b = ⊤) {c : Set C} (hc : Algebra.adjoin A c = ⊤)
    (u : B →ₐ[A] C) (Ψ : C →ₐ[A] S ⊗[A] B) (hΨb : ∀ x ∈ b, Ψ (u x) = 1 ⊗ₜ x)
    (hΨc : ∀ x ∈ c, Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := S) S u (Ψ x) = 1 ⊗ₜ x) :
    Function.Bijective (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := S) S u) := by
  set v : S ⊗[A] C →ₐ[S] S ⊗[A] B :=
    Algebra.TensorProduct.lift (Algebra.ofId S (S ⊗[A] B)) Ψ (fun _ _ ↦ Commute.all _ _) with hv
  have hone : ((1 : S) ⊗ₜ[A] (1 : B)) = (1 : S ⊗[A] B) := rfl
  have hvc : ∀ x : C, v ((1 : S) ⊗ₜ[A] x) = Ψ x := by
    intro x
    rw [hv]
    simp [hone]
  have hleft : v.comp (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := S) S u) = AlgHom.id S (S ⊗[A] B) := by
    refine algHom_ext_of_adjoin_eq_top hb fun x hx ↦ ?_
    have h1 : Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := S) S u ((1 : S) ⊗ₜ[A] x)
        = (1 : S) ⊗ₜ[A] u x := by simp
    rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, h1, hvc, AlgHom.id_apply]
    exact hΨb x hx
  have hright : (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := S) S u).comp v
      = AlgHom.id S (S ⊗[A] C) := by
    refine algHom_ext_of_adjoin_eq_top hc fun x hx ↦ ?_
    rw [AlgHom.comp_apply, hvc, AlgHom.id_apply]
    exact hΨc x hx
  exact ⟨fun x y hxy ↦ by
      have h1 := AlgHom.congr_fun hleft x
      have h2 := AlgHom.congr_fun hleft y
      simp only [AlgHom.comp_apply, AlgHom.id_apply] at h1 h2
      rw [← h1, ← h2, hxy],
    fun z ↦ ⟨v z, by simpa using AlgHom.congr_fun hright z⟩⟩

end Ext

section Naturality

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {S : Type*} [CommRing S] [Algebra A S]
  {T : Type*} [CommRing T] [Algebra A T] {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
  {C : Type*} [CommRing C] [Algebra A C]

/-- `Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor` is `LinearMap.rTensor` on underlying modules. -/
private theorem coe_rTensor (φ : S →ₐ[A] T) (z : S ⊗[A] B) :
    Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B φ z = LinearMap.rTensor B φ.toLinearMap z := by
  induction z with
  | tmul x y => simp
  | add z₁ z₂ h₁ h₂ => simp [h₁, h₂]

/-- Base change along `S → T` commutes with base change along `B → C`. -/
private theorem rTensor_lTensor_apply (φ : S →ₐ[A] T) (u : B →ₐ[A] C) (z : S ⊗[A] B) :
    Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C φ (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := S) S u z) =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := T) T u (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B φ z) := by
  induction z with
  | tmul x y => simp
  | add z₁ z₂ h₁ h₂ => simp [h₁, h₂]

/-- Base change is functorial in the ring. -/
private theorem rTensor_rTensor_apply {U : Type*} [CommRing U] [Algebra A U]
    (φ : S →ₐ[A] T) (ψ : T →ₐ[A] U) (z : S ⊗[A] B) :
    Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B ψ (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B φ z) =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (ψ.comp φ) z := by
  exact (AlgHom.congr_fun (Algebra.TensorProduct.map_comp ψ φ (.id A B) (.id A B)) z).symm

/-- Base change is functorial in the ring, for maps that agree pointwise. -/
private theorem rTensor_rTensor_of_comp_eq {U : Type*} [CommRing U] [Algebra A U]
    (φ : S →ₐ[A] T) (ψ : T →ₐ[A] U) (χ : S →ₐ[A] U) (h : ∀ x, ψ (φ x) = χ x) (z : S ⊗[A] B) :
    Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B ψ (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B φ z) =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B χ z := by
  rw [rTensor_rTensor_apply, show ψ.comp φ = χ from AlgHom.ext h]

end Naturality

section System

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
  {ι : Type t} [Preorder ι] [Nonempty ι] [IsDirectedOrder ι]
  {G : ι → Type s} [∀ i, CommRing (G i)] [∀ i, Algebra A (G i)]
  {f : ∀ i j, i ≤ j → G i →ₐ[A] G j} [DirectedSystem G fun i j h ↦ ⇑(f i j h)]
  {R : Type r} [CommRing R] [Algebra A R] {g : ∀ i, G i →ₐ[A] R}
  {hg : ∀ i j h x, g j (f i j h x) = g i x}
  (hR : Function.Bijective (DirectLimit.Algebra.lift G f R g hg))

omit [Nonempty ι] [IsDirectedOrder ι] in
private theorem comp_transition {i j k : ι} (h₁ : i ≤ j) (h₂ : j ≤ k) :
    (f j k h₂).comp (f i j h₁) = f i k (h₁.trans h₂) :=
  AlgHom.ext fun x ↦ DirectedSystem.map_map (f := fun i j h ↦ ⇑(f i j h)) h₁ h₂ x

omit [Nonempty ι] [IsDirectedOrder ι] in
private theorem transition_self {i : ι} (h : i ≤ i) (x : G i) : f i i h x = x :=
  DirectedSystem.map_self (f := fun i j h ↦ ⇑(f i j h)) x

omit [Nonempty ι] [IsDirectedOrder ι] in
/-- The transition map from a stage to itself acts as the identity after base change. -/
private theorem rTensor_transition_self {M : Type*} [CommRing M] [Algebra A M] {i : ι} (h : i ≤ i)
    (z : G i ⊗[A] M) : Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor M (f i i h) z = z := by
  have hid : f i i h = AlgHom.id A (G i) := AlgHom.ext fun x ↦ transition_self h x
  rw [hid]
  simp

include hR

/-- Every element of the colimit comes from some stage. -/
private theorem exists_eq_apply (x : R) : ∃ i y, g i y = x := by
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hR.surjective x
  obtain ⟨i, y, rfl⟩ := DirectLimit.exists_eq_mk _ z
  exact ⟨i, y, hz⟩

/-- An element dying in the colimit dies at a later stage. -/
private theorem exists_map_eq_zero {i : ι} {x : G i} (hx : g i x = 0) :
    ∃ j, ∃ h : i ≤ j, f i j h x = 0 := by
  have hz : (⟦⟨i, x⟩⟧ : DirectLimit G f) = 0 := hR.injective (by simpa using hx)
  simpa using (DirectLimit.exists_eq_zero (f := f) ⟨i, x⟩).mp hz

section Tensor

variable (M : Type*) [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]

private theorem exists_lRTensor_eq (z : R ⊗[A] M) :
    ∃ (i : ι) (y : G i ⊗[A] M), LinearMap.rTensor M (g i).toLinearMap y = z := by
  have hc : ∀ (i j : ι) (h : i ≤ j),
      (g j).toLinearMap ∘ₗ (f i j h).toLinearMap = (g i).toLinearMap :=
    fun i j h ↦ LinearMap.ext fun x ↦ hg i j h x
  induction z with
  | tmul x m =>
      obtain ⟨i, y, rfl⟩ := exists_eq_apply hR x
      exact ⟨i, y ⊗ₜ m, by simp⟩
  | add z₁ z₂ h₁ h₂ =>
      obtain ⟨i₁, y₁, rfl⟩ := h₁
      obtain ⟨i₂, y₂, rfl⟩ := h₂
      obtain ⟨k, hk₁, hk₂⟩ := exists_ge_ge i₁ i₂
      refine ⟨k, LinearMap.rTensor M (f i₁ k hk₁).toLinearMap y₁ +
        LinearMap.rTensor M (f i₂ k hk₂).toLinearMap y₂, ?_⟩
      rw [map_add, ← LinearMap.rTensor_comp_apply, ← LinearMap.rTensor_comp_apply, hc, hc]

private theorem exists_lRTensor_map_eq_zero {i : ι} (y : G i ⊗[A] M)
    (hy : LinearMap.rTensor M (g i).toLinearMap y = 0) :
    ∃ (j : ι) (h : i ≤ j), LinearMap.rTensor M (f i j h).toLinearMap y = 0 := by
  classical
  have hds : DirectedSystem G fun i j h ↦ ⇑((fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) i j h) :=
    inferInstanceAs (DirectedSystem G fun i j h ↦ ⇑(f i j h))
  have hLof : ∀ (k : ι) (x : G k),
      Module.DirectLimit.lift A ι G (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap)
          (fun i ↦ (g i).toLinearMap) (fun i j h x ↦ hg i j h x)
        (Module.DirectLimit.of A ι G (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) k x) = g k x :=
    fun k x ↦ Module.DirectLimit.lift_of _ _ x
  have hinj : Function.Injective (Module.DirectLimit.lift A ι G
      (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) (fun i ↦ (g i).toLinearMap)
      (fun i j h x ↦ hg i j h x)) := by
    rw [← LinearMap.ker_eq_bot, LinearMap.ker_eq_bot']
    intro z hz
    obtain ⟨k, x, rfl⟩ := Module.DirectLimit.exists_of (R := A) (ι := ι)
      (f := fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) z
    rw [hLof] at hz
    obtain ⟨j, hkj, hj⟩ := exists_map_eq_zero hR hz
    have hj' : (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) k j hkj x = 0 := hj
    rw [← Module.DirectLimit.of_f (f := fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) (hij := hkj), hj',
      map_zero]
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (Module.DirectLimit.lift A ι G
      (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) (fun i ↦ (g i).toLinearMap)
      (fun i j h x ↦ hg i j h x)) := by
    intro z
    obtain ⟨k, x, hx⟩ := exists_eq_apply hR z
    exact ⟨Module.DirectLimit.of A ι G (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) k x,
      (hLof k x).trans hx⟩
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ : ∃ e : Module.DirectLimit G (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) ≃ₗ[A] R,
      ∀ (k : ι) (x : G k),
        e (Module.DirectLimit.of A ι G (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) k x) = g k x :=
    ⟨LinearEquiv.ofBijective _ ⟨hinj, hsurj⟩, hLof⟩
  have hgi : (g i).toLinearMap =
      e.toLinearMap ∘ₗ Module.DirectLimit.of A ι G (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) i :=
    LinearMap.ext fun x ↦ (he i x).symm
  have h0 : LinearMap.rTensor M
      (Module.DirectLimit.of A ι G (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) i) y = 0 := by
    have h1 : LinearMap.rTensor M e.toLinearMap (LinearMap.rTensor M
        (Module.DirectLimit.of A ι G (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) i) y) = 0 := by
      rw [← LinearMap.rTensor_comp_apply, ← hgi, hy]
    have h2 := congrArg (LinearMap.rTensor M e.symm.toLinearMap) h1
    rw [← LinearMap.rTensor_comp_apply, map_zero] at h2
    have h3 : e.symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ e.toLinearMap = LinearMap.id :=
      LinearMap.ext fun x ↦ e.symm_apply_apply x
    rwa [h3, LinearMap.rTensor_id, LinearMap.id_apply] at h2
  have h4 := congrArg (TensorProduct.directLimitLeft (fun i j h ↦ (f i j h).toLinearMap) M) h0
  rw [TensorProduct.directLimitLeft_rTensor_of, map_zero] at h4
  exact Module.DirectLimit.of.zero_exact h4

end Tensor

section AlgTensor

variable (M : Type*) [CommRing M] [Algebra A M]

/-- `R ⊗[A] M` is the colimit of the `G i ⊗[A] M`: surjectivity. -/
private theorem exists_rTensor_eq (z : R ⊗[A] M) :
    ∃ (i : ι) (y : G i ⊗[A] M), Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor M (g i) y = z := by
  obtain ⟨i, y, hy⟩ := exists_lRTensor_eq hR M z
  exact ⟨i, y, (coe_rTensor _ _).trans hy⟩

/-- `R ⊗[A] M` is the colimit of the `G i ⊗[A] M`: injectivity. -/
private theorem exists_rTensor_map_eq {i : ι} (y y' : G i ⊗[A] M)
    (hy : Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor M (g i) y = Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor M (g i) y') :
    ∃ (j : ι) (h : i ≤ j), Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor M (f i j h) y =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor M (f i j h) y' := by
  have h0 : LinearMap.rTensor M (g i).toLinearMap (y - y') = 0 := by
    rw [map_sub, ← coe_rTensor, ← coe_rTensor, hy, sub_self]
  obtain ⟨j, h, hj⟩ := exists_lRTensor_map_eq_zero hR M (y - y') h0
  refine ⟨j, h, ?_⟩
  rw [map_sub, ← coe_rTensor, ← coe_rTensor] at hj
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp hj

end AlgTensor

/-- Finitely many polynomial relations that elements of a stage satisfy over `R` are satisfied by
their images at a later stage. -/
private theorem exists_aeval_eq_zero {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] {n : ℕ} {i₀ : ι}
    (Z : Fin n → G i₀ ⊗[A] B) (E : Finset (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A))
    (hE : ∀ e ∈ E, Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i₀) (MvPolynomial.aeval
      (fun m ↦ Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ i₀ le_rfl) (Z m)) e) = 0) :
    ∃ j, ∃ hij : i₀ ≤ j, ∀ e ∈ E,
      MvPolynomial.aeval (fun m ↦ Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j hij) (Z m)) e = 0 := by
  have hstep : ∀ (j k : ι) (hj : i₀ ≤ j) (hk : i₀ ≤ k) (hjk : j ≤ k),
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f j k hjk)).comp
        (MvPolynomial.aeval fun m ↦ Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j hj) (Z m))
      = MvPolynomial.aeval fun m ↦ Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ k hk) (Z m) := by
    intro j k hj hk hjk
    rw [MvPolynomial.comp_aeval]
    congr 1
    funext m
    rw [rTensor_rTensor_apply, comp_transition]
  have hexE : ∀ e ∈ E, ∃ j : ι, ∃ h : i₀ ≤ j,
      MvPolynomial.aeval (fun m ↦ Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j h) (Z m)) e = 0 := by
    intro e he
    obtain ⟨j, h, hj⟩ := exists_rTensor_map_eq hR B _ 0 (by rw [hE e he, map_zero])
    refine ⟨j, h, ?_⟩
    rw [← AlgHom.congr_fun (hstep i₀ j le_rfl h h) e]
    simpa using hj
  have hmono : ∀ (j k : ι) (h : i₀ ≤ j) (hjk : j ≤ k) (e : MvPolynomial (Fin n) A),
      MvPolynomial.aeval (fun m ↦ Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j h) (Z m)) e = 0 →
      MvPolynomial.aeval
        (fun m ↦ Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ k (h.trans hjk)) (Z m)) e = 0 := by
    intro j k h hjk e he
    rw [← AlgHom.congr_fun (hstep j k h (h.trans hjk) hjk) e]
    simp [he]
  exact exists_forall_le_of_forall_exists i₀ E _ hmono hexE

/-- The heart of item (3): an `A`-algebra map from a finitely presented `A`-algebra `C` into
`R ⊗[A] B` factors through some `G i ⊗[A] B`. -/
private theorem exists_lift_of_finitePresentation {B C : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [CommRing C] [Algebra A C] [Algebra.FinitePresentation A C] (w : C →ₐ[A] R ⊗[A] B) :
    ∃ (i : ι) (ψ : C →ₐ[A] G i ⊗[A] B),
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i)).comp ψ = w := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨n, π, hπ, hfg⟩ := Algebra.FinitePresentation.out (R := A) (A := C)
  obtain ⟨E, hE⟩ := hfg
  choose i₁ z₁ hz₁ using fun m : Fin n ↦ exists_rTensor_eq hR B (w (π (MvPolynomial.X m)))
  obtain ⟨i₀, hi₀⟩ := (Finset.image i₁ Finset.univ).exists_le
  have hle : ∀ m : Fin n, i₁ m ≤ i₀ := fun m ↦
    hi₀ _ (Finset.mem_image_of_mem _ (Finset.mem_univ m))
  obtain ⟨Z, hZg⟩ : ∃ Z : Fin n → G i₀ ⊗[A] B,
      ∀ m, Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i₀) (Z m) = w (π (MvPolynomial.X m)) := by
    refine ⟨fun m ↦ Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f (i₁ m) i₀ (hle m)) (z₁ m), fun m ↦ ?_⟩
    rw [rTensor_rTensor_of_comp_eq _ (g i₀) _ (hg _ _ _), hz₁ m]
  have ha : ∀ (j : ι) (h : i₀ ≤ j), (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g j)).comp
      (MvPolynomial.aeval fun m ↦ Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j h) (Z m))
      = w.comp π := by
    intro j h
    rw [MvPolynomial.comp_aeval, MvPolynomial.aeval_unique (w.comp π)]
    congr 1
    funext m
    rw [rTensor_rTensor_of_comp_eq _ (g j) _ (hg _ _ _)]
    exact hZg m
  obtain ⟨j, hij, hzero⟩ := exists_aeval_eq_zero hR Z E fun e he ↦ by
    have hπe : π e = 0 := by
      have : e ∈ RingHom.ker π.toRingHom := by
        rw [← hE]
        exact Ideal.subset_span he
      exact RingHom.mem_ker.mp this
    simpa [hπe] using AlgHom.congr_fun (ha i₀ le_rfl) e
  refine ⟨j, π.liftOfSurjective hπ
    (MvPolynomial.aeval fun m ↦ Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j hij) (Z m)) fun p hp ↦ ?_,
    AlgHom.ext fun c ↦ ?_⟩
  · have hpk : p ∈ Ideal.span (E : Set (MvPolynomial (Fin n) A)) := by
      rw [hE]
      exact hp
    refine Submodule.span_induction (p := fun x _ ↦
      MvPolynomial.aeval (fun m ↦ Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j hij) (Z m)) x = 0)
      (fun x hx ↦ hzero x hx) (by simp) (fun x y _ _ hx hy ↦ by simp [hx, hy])
      (fun a x _ hx ↦ by simp [hx]) hpk
  · obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := hπ c
    rw [AlgHom.comp_apply]
    refine (congrArg _ (π.liftOfSurjective_apply hπ _ _ p)).trans ?_
    exact AlgHom.congr_fun (ha j hij) p

/-- Item (1) of Stacks 05N8: two maps out of a finite type algebra that agree after base change
to `R` agree after base change to some `G i`. -/
private theorem lTensor_eq_of_lTensor_eq {B C : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra A C] [Algebra.FiniteType A B] (u u' : B →ₐ[A] C)
    (huu' : Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u') :
    ∃ i, Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G i) (G i) u =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G i) (G i) u' := by
  obtain ⟨tB, htB⟩ := Algebra.FiniteType.out (R := A) (A := B)
  have hmono : ∀ ⦃j k : ι⦄, j ≤ k → ∀ b : B,
      ((1 : G j) ⊗ₜ[A] u b = (1 : G j) ⊗ₜ[A] u' b) →
      ((1 : G k) ⊗ₜ[A] u b = (1 : G k) ⊗ₜ[A] u' b) := fun j k hjk b hb ↦ by
    simpa using congrArg (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (f j k hjk)) hb
  have hex : ∀ b ∈ tB, ∃ j : ι, (1 : G j) ⊗ₜ[A] u b = (1 : G j) ⊗ₜ[A] u' b := by
    intro b _
    have hRb : Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (g (Classical.arbitrary ι))
          ((1 : G (Classical.arbitrary ι)) ⊗ₜ[A] u b)
        = Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (g (Classical.arbitrary ι))
          ((1 : G (Classical.arbitrary ι)) ⊗ₜ[A] u' b) := by
      simpa using AlgHom.congr_fun huu' ((1 : R) ⊗ₜ[A] b)
    obtain ⟨j, h, hj⟩ := exists_rTensor_map_eq hR C _ _ hRb
    exact ⟨j, by simpa using hj⟩
  obtain ⟨j, -, hj⟩ := exists_forall_of_forall_exists (Classical.arbitrary ι) tB _ hmono hex
  exact ⟨j, algHom_ext_of_adjoin_eq_top htB fun b hb ↦ by
    simpa using hj b (by simpa using hb)⟩

/-- Item (2) of Stacks 05N8: a map into a finite type algebra that is surjective after base change
to `R` is surjective after base change to some `G i`. -/
private theorem lTensor_surjective_of_lTensor_surjective {B C : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [CommRing C] [Algebra A C] [Algebra.FiniteType A C] (u : B →ₐ[A] C)
    (husurj : Function.Surjective (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u)) :
    ∃ i, Function.Surjective (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G i) (G i) u) := by
  obtain ⟨tC, htC⟩ := Algebra.FiniteType.out (R := A) (A := C)
  have hmono : ∀ ⦃j k : ι⦄, j ≤ k → ∀ c : C,
      (∃ z : G j ⊗[A] B, Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G j) (G j) u z = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] c) →
      (∃ z : G k ⊗[A] B, Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G k) (G k) u z = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] c) := by
    rintro j k hjk c ⟨z, hz⟩
    refine ⟨Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f j k hjk) z, ?_⟩
    rw [← rTensor_lTensor_apply, hz]
    simp
  have hex : ∀ c ∈ tC, ∃ j : ι,
      ∃ z : G j ⊗[A] B, Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G j) (G j) u z = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] c := by
    intro c _
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := husurj ((1 : R) ⊗ₜ[A] c)
    obtain ⟨i, z, hz⟩ := exists_rTensor_eq hR B y
    have key : Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (g i)
          (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G i) (G i) u z)
        = Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (g i) ((1 : G i) ⊗ₜ[A] c) := by
      rw [rTensor_lTensor_apply, hz, hy]
      simp
    obtain ⟨j, h, hj⟩ := exists_rTensor_map_eq hR C _ _ key
    refine ⟨j, Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i j h) z, ?_⟩
    rw [← rTensor_lTensor_apply]
    simpa using hj
  obtain ⟨j, -, hj⟩ := exists_forall_of_forall_exists (Classical.arbitrary ι) tC _ hmono hex
  refine ⟨j, ?_⟩
  rw [← AlgHom.range_eq_top]
  refine subalgebra_eq_top_of_one_tmul_mem htC _ fun c hc ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hj c (by simpa using hc)
  exact ⟨z, hz⟩

/-- Item (3) of Stacks 05N8: an `R`-algebra map `R ⊗[A] C → R ⊗[A] B` out of a finitely presented
`C` comes from some `G i ⊗[A] C → G i ⊗[A] B`. -/
private theorem exists_baseChange_lift {B C : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra A C] [Algebra.FinitePresentation A C] (v : R ⊗[A] C →ₐ[R] R ⊗[A] B) :
    ∃ (i : ι) (vᵢ : G i ⊗[A] C →ₐ[G i] G i ⊗[A] B),
      (v.restrictScalars A).comp (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (g i)) =
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i)).comp (vᵢ.restrictScalars A) := by
  obtain ⟨i, ψ, hψ⟩ := exists_lift_of_finitePresentation hR
    ((v.restrictScalars A).comp Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight)
  refine ⟨i, Algebra.TensorProduct.lift (Algebra.ofId (G i) (G i ⊗[A] B)) ψ
    (fun _ _ ↦ Commute.all _ _), Algebra.TensorProduct.ext ?_ ?_⟩
  · refine AlgHom.ext fun x ↦ ?_
    have hx : (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft : G i →ₐ[A] G i ⊗[A] C) x
        = algebraMap (G i) (G i ⊗[A] C) x := by
      simp [Algebra.TensorProduct.algebraMap_apply]
    have hLx : Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (g i) (algebraMap (G i) (G i ⊗[A] C) x)
        = algebraMap R (R ⊗[A] C) (g i x) := by
      simp [Algebra.TensorProduct.algebraMap_apply]
    have hRx : Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i) (algebraMap (G i) (G i ⊗[A] B) x)
        = algebraMap R (R ⊗[A] B) (g i x) := by
      simp [Algebra.TensorProduct.algebraMap_apply]
    simp only [AlgHom.comp_apply, hx, hLx]
    rw [show (AlgHom.restrictScalars A v) (algebraMap R (R ⊗[A] C) (g i x))
          = algebraMap R (R ⊗[A] B) (g i x) from v.commutes (g i x),
      show (AlgHom.restrictScalars A (Algebra.TensorProduct.lift
            (Algebra.ofId (G i) (G i ⊗[A] B)) ψ (fun _ _ ↦ Commute.all _ _)))
          (algebraMap (G i) (G i ⊗[A] C) x) = algebraMap (G i) (G i ⊗[A] B) x from
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.lift (Algebra.ofId (G i) (G i ⊗[A] B)) ψ
          (fun _ _ ↦ Commute.all _ _)).commutes x, hRx]
  · refine AlgHom.ext fun c ↦ ?_
    have hvc : Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i) (ψ c) = v ((1 : R) ⊗ₜ[A] c) :=
      AlgHom.congr_fun hψ c
    have h1 : ((1 : G i) ⊗ₜ[A] (1 : B)) = (1 : G i ⊗[A] B) := rfl
    simpa [h1] using hvc.symm

/-- If `ψ` inverts `u` on finitely many generators after base change to `R`, it does so after base
change to some later stage. -/
private theorem exists_stage_inverse_on_generators {B C : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [CommRing C] [Algebra A C] {i₀ : ι} (u : B →ₐ[A] C) (ψ : C →ₐ[A] G i₀ ⊗[A] B)
    (tB : Finset B) (tC : Finset C)
    (hB : ∀ b : B, Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i₀) (ψ (u b))
      = Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i₀) ((1 : G i₀) ⊗ₜ[A] b))
    (hC : ∀ c : C, Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (g i₀)
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G i₀) (G i₀) u (ψ c))
      = Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (g i₀) ((1 : G i₀) ⊗ₜ[A] c)) :
    ∃ j, ∃ hij : i₀ ≤ j,
      (∀ b ∈ tB, Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j hij) (ψ (u b)) = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] b) ∧
      ∀ c ∈ tC, Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G j) (G j) u
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j hij) (ψ c)) = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] c := by
  have hBmono : ∀ (j k : ι) (h : i₀ ≤ j) (hjk : j ≤ k) (b : B),
      Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j h) (ψ (u b)) = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] b →
      Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ k (h.trans hjk)) (ψ (u b)) = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] b := by
    intro j k h hjk b hb
    have hb' := congrArg (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f j k hjk)) hb
    rw [rTensor_rTensor_apply, comp_transition] at hb'
    simpa using hb'
  have hCmono : ∀ (j k : ι) (h : i₀ ≤ j) (hjk : j ≤ k) (c : C),
      Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G j) (G j) u
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j h) (ψ c)) = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] c →
      Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G k) (G k) u
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ k (h.trans hjk)) (ψ c)) = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] c := by
    intro j k h hjk c hc
    have hc' := congrArg (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (f j k hjk)) hc
    rw [rTensor_lTensor_apply, rTensor_rTensor_apply, comp_transition] at hc'
    simpa using hc'
  have hBex : ∀ b ∈ tB, ∃ j : ι,
      ∃ h : i₀ ≤ j, Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j h) (ψ (u b)) = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] b := by
    intro b _
    obtain ⟨j, h, hj⟩ := exists_rTensor_map_eq hR B _ _ (hB b)
    exact ⟨j, h, by simpa using hj⟩
  have hCex : ∀ c ∈ tC, ∃ j : ι, ∃ h : i₀ ≤ j,
      Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G j) (G j) u
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j h) (ψ c)) = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] c := by
    intro c _
    obtain ⟨j, h, hj⟩ := exists_rTensor_map_eq hR C _ _ (hC c)
    refine ⟨j, h, ?_⟩
    rw [← rTensor_lTensor_apply]
    simpa using hj
  obtain ⟨j₁, hij₁, hB₁⟩ := exists_forall_le_of_forall_exists i₀ tB _ hBmono hBex
  obtain ⟨j₂, hij₂, hC₂⟩ := exists_forall_le_of_forall_exists i₀ tC _ hCmono hCex
  obtain ⟨j, hj₁, hj₂⟩ := exists_ge_ge j₁ j₂
  exact ⟨j, hij₁.trans hj₁, fun b hb ↦ hBmono _ _ _ hj₁ b (hB₁ b hb),
    fun c hc ↦ hCmono _ _ _ hj₂ c (hC₂ c hc)⟩

/-- Item (4) of Stacks 05N8: a map from a finite type to a finitely presented algebra that is
bijective after base change to `R` is bijective after base change to some `G i`. -/
private theorem lTensor_bijective_of_lTensor_bijective {B C : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [CommRing C] [Algebra A C] [Algebra.FiniteType A B] [Algebra.FinitePresentation A C]
    (u : B →ₐ[A] C) (hbij : Function.Bijective (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u)) :
    ∃ i, Function.Bijective (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G i) (G i) u) := by
  obtain ⟨tB, htB⟩ := Algebra.FiniteType.out (R := A) (A := B)
  obtain ⟨tC, htC⟩ := Algebra.FiniteType.out (R := A) (A := C)
  let E := AlgEquiv.ofBijective (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u) hbij
  obtain ⟨e, heU, hUe⟩ : ∃ e : R ⊗[A] C →ₐ[R] R ⊗[A] B,
      (∀ z, Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u (e z) = z) ∧
      (∀ z, e (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u z) = z) :=
    ⟨(E.symm : R ⊗[A] C →ₐ[R] R ⊗[A] B), E.apply_symm_apply, E.symm_apply_apply⟩
  obtain ⟨i₀, ψ, hψ⟩ := exists_lift_of_finitePresentation hR
    ((e.restrictScalars A).comp Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight)
  have hψc : ∀ c : C, Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i₀) (ψ c) = e ((1 : R) ⊗ₜ[A] c) :=
    fun c ↦ by simpa using AlgHom.congr_fun hψ c
  -- the generators of `B`: `ψ (u b)` and `1 ⊗ b` agree over `R`
  have hB : ∀ b : B, Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i₀) (ψ (u b))
      = Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i₀) ((1 : G i₀) ⊗ₜ[A] b) := by
    intro b
    have h2 : Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u ((1 : R) ⊗ₜ[A] b)
        = (1 : R) ⊗ₜ[A] u b := by simp
    rw [hψc, ← h2, hUe]
    simp
  -- the generators of `C`: `u (ψ c)` and `1 ⊗ c` agree over `R`
  have hC : ∀ c : C, Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (g i₀)
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G i₀) (G i₀) u (ψ c))
      = Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (g i₀) ((1 : G i₀) ⊗ₜ[A] c) := by
    intro c
    rw [rTensor_lTensor_apply, hψc, heU]
    simp
  obtain ⟨j, hij, hBj, hCj⟩ := exists_stage_inverse_on_generators hR u ψ tB tC hB hC
  exact ⟨j, lTensor_bijective_of_generators htB htC u
    ((Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (f i₀ j hij)).comp ψ) (fun b hb ↦ hBj b hb)
    (fun c hc ↦ hCj c hc)⟩

end System

/-- **Stacks 05N8.** -/
public theorem solution {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    {B : Type v} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] {C : Type w} [CommRing C] [Algebra A C]
    {ι : Type t} [Preorder ι] [Nonempty ι] [IsDirectedOrder ι]
    {G : ι → Type s} [∀ i, CommRing (G i)] [∀ i, Algebra A (G i)]
    (f : ∀ i j, i ≤ j → G i →ₐ[A] G j) [DirectedSystem G fun i j h ↦ ⇑(f i j h)]
    {R : Type r} [CommRing R] [Algebra A R] (g : ∀ i, G i →ₐ[A] R)
    (hg : ∀ i j h x, g j (f i j h x) = g i x)
    (hR : Function.Bijective (DirectLimit.Algebra.lift G f R g hg)) :
    (Algebra.FiniteType A B → ∀ u u' : B →ₐ[A] C,
        Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u = Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u' →
        ∃ i, Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G i) (G i) u =
          Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G i) (G i) u') ∧
    (Algebra.FiniteType A C → ∀ u : B →ₐ[A] C,
        Function.Surjective (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u) →
        ∃ i, Function.Surjective (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G i) (G i) u)) ∧
    (Algebra.FinitePresentation A C → ∀ v : R ⊗[A] C →ₐ[R] R ⊗[A] B,
        ∃ (i : ι) (vᵢ : G i ⊗[A] C →ₐ[G i] G i ⊗[A] B),
          (v.restrictScalars A).comp (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor C (g i)) =
            (Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i)).comp (vᵢ.restrictScalars A)) ∧
    (Algebra.FiniteType A B → Algebra.FinitePresentation A C → ∀ u : B →ₐ[A] C,
        Function.Bijective (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R) R u) →
        ∃ i, Function.Bijective (Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := G i) (G i) u)) :=
  ⟨fun _ u u' ↦ lTensor_eq_of_lTensor_eq hR u u',
    fun _ u ↦ lTensor_surjective_of_lTensor_surjective hR u,
    fun _ v ↦ exists_baseChange_lift hR v,
    fun _ _ u ↦ lTensor_bijective_of_lTensor_bijective hR u⟩

end Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraMapDescent

/-!
# Algebra maps over a directed colimit of rings come from a finite level

Let `A` be a ring, let `B`, `C` be `A`-algebras and let `R = colim_i R_i` be a directed colimit
of `A`-algebras. Base change along `A → R` factors through each `A → R_i`, and the four items
below say that a property of, or a piece of data over, the base change to `R` is already present
over some `R_i`, as soon as the algebras involved are of finite type, resp. of finite
presentation, over `A`:

1. if `B` is of finite type and two `A`-algebra maps `u, u' : B → C` have equal base changes to
   `R`, their base changes to some `R_i` are equal;
2. if `C` is of finite type and the base change of `u : B → C` to `R` is surjective, then its
   base change to some `R_i` is surjective;
3. if `C` is of finite presentation, every `R`-algebra map `C ⊗_A R → B ⊗_A R` is the base
   change of an `R_i`-algebra map `C ⊗_A R_i → B ⊗_A R_i` for some `i`;
4. if `B` is of finite type, `C` of finite presentation, and the base change of `u` to `R` is an
   isomorphism, then its base change to some `R_i` is an isomorphism.

The mechanism in each case is that `B ⊗_A R = colim_i B ⊗_A R_i`: finitely many generators, and
in items (3) and (4) finitely many relations, are caught at a finite level. Together with the
analogue for modules (Lemma `05LI`) this is what makes the category of finitely presented
`R`-algebras the colimit of the categories of finitely presented `R_i`-algebras (Lemma `05N9`).

## Main results

* `Algebra.TensorProduct.exists_of_directLimit`: the four items above, as the four conjuncts of
  one statement about one directed system.

## Implementation notes

Base change is the concrete tensor product: `B ⊗_A R` is spelled `R ⊗[A] B`, with the scalars on
the left, since that is the factor `Algebra.TensorProduct.leftAlgebra` makes the ring act on, and
`u ⊗ 1 : B ⊗_A R_i → C ⊗_A R_i` is the named combinator
`Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor (S := R_i) R_i u`, an `R_i`-algebra map. The comparison maps
`B ⊗_A R_i → B ⊗_A R` are `Algebra.TensorProduct.rTensor B (g i)`, `A`-algebra maps.

"`R = colim_i R_i` is a directed colimit of `A`-algebras" is the data of a directed system (`ι` a
directed preorder, `G : ι → Type*` a family of `A`-algebras, transition maps `f i j` forming a
`DirectedSystem`) together with a compatible family `g i : G i →ₐ[A] R` whose induced map out of
`DirectLimit G f` is bijective. This is the spelling of the sibling Lemma `00QN`, and it pins the
comparison map instead of asserting an abstract isomorphism `colim_i G i ≃ₐ[A] R`. The two
elementary consequences a proof uses are `DirectLimit.exists_eq_mk`, that every element of the
colimit comes from some `G i`, and `DirectLimit.exists_eq_zero`, that an element of `G i` dying
in the colimit already dies in some `G j`. `Nonempty ι` is not an extra assumption on the system
but a requirement of the algebra structure on `DirectLimit G f`, without which the comparison map
cannot be written down.

Item (3)'s conclusion `v = v_i ⊗ 1` is the commuting square
`v ∘ rTensor C (g i) = rTensor B (g i) ∘ v_i` of `A`-algebra maps `G i ⊗[A] C → R ⊗[A] B`, i.e.
compatibility of `v` and `v_i` with the comparison maps. This is equivalent to `v` being the base
change of `v_i` along `g i`, and it determines `v` from `v_i`, since an `R`-algebra map out of
`R ⊗[A] C` is determined by its values on the elements `1 ⊗ c` and the square prescribes them.
Stating it this way avoids transporting `v_i` along the canonical isomorphism
`R ⊗_{G i} (G i ⊗[A] C) ≃ₐ[R] R ⊗[A] C`.

The four items are the four conjuncts of a single statement about a single directed system, each
carrying only the finiteness hypothesis it uses, so that no item is weakened. The base ring `A`
is arbitrary, which is what makes item (1) already give the statement about `R_i`-algebra maps
between base changes that Lemma `05N9` applies it for: instantiate it with `A := R_i` and the
system `(R_j)_{j ≥ i}` of `R_i`-algebras.

Faithfulness. (1) No hypothesis is idle. The colimit hypothesis `hR` is used in every item:
without it the one-object system `G = fun _ ↦ ℤ` with `g = algebraMap ℤ ℤ[1/2]` would make item
(2) say that surjectivity of `u ⊗ 1` over `R = ℤ[1/2]` descends to `u` itself, which fails for
`A = B = ℤ` and `C = ℤ[1/2] = ℤ[y]/(2y - 1)`. Each finiteness hypothesis is used as well: over
`A = k[t_1, t_2, …]` with `G i = A/(t_1, …, t_i)` and `R = k`, item (1) fails for
`B = A[x_1, x_2, …]`, `C = A` and `u x_n = t_n`, `u' x_n = 0`, which agree over `R` but over no
`G i`; and over `A = ℤ` with `G n = ℤ[1/n!]` and `R = ℚ`, item (2) fails for `B = ℤ` and `C = ℚ`,
where `u ⊗ 1` is bijective over `R` but `ℤ[1/n!] → ℚ` is surjective for no `n`. (2) The scalars
and base are the source's: `u, u' : B →ₐ[A] C` are `A`-algebra maps, `v` is an `R`-algebra map
and `v_i` an `R_i`-algebra map, and the finiteness hypotheses are over `A`. (3) The canonical
maps are pinned: `u ⊗ 1` is `Algebra.TensorProduct.lTensor`, `R = colim_i R_i` is bijectivity of
`DirectLimit.Algebra.lift G f R g hg`, and item (3)'s `v = v_i ⊗ 1` is the commuting square
above, not a bare existence claim. (4) The instantiation is not degenerate: in the system
`A = k[t_1, t_2, …]`, `G i = A/(t_1, …, t_i)`, `R = k` above, item (1) has content for `B = A[x]`
with `u x = t_1`, `u' x = 0` (equal over `G i` exactly for `i ≥ 1`), item (2) for `B = A`,
`C = A[y]/(t_1 y - 1)` (where `C ⊗_A G i = 0` exactly for `i ≥ 1`), and item (4) for `B = A`,
`C = A/(t_1)`; and item (3) has content for `A = ℤ`, `G n = ℤ[1/n!]`, `R = ℚ`, `B = ℤ[x]`,
`C = ℤ[y]` and `v : y ↦ x/N`, which comes from level `n` exactly when `N` divides a power of
`n!`.

